{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood","id":1070506,"title":"What to do with a Captured Dragonblood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T00:11:15-07:00","id":1070506,"title":"What to do with a Captured Dragonblood","content":"Alright, so my players - who are pretty much a merry band of Solar pirates - have managed to capture a Water-Aspect Dragonblood after raiding his ship heading from the north West to the Blessed Isle. The issue is, I'm not entirely sure what to do with the character now. He's wise enough to know that just running from a group of 6 Solars is unlikely to end well for him, especially when one has a giant hawk he can ride on. I don't just want him to sit around like a proverbial lemon, though.<br /> <br /> Advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:22:05-07:00","id":1070509,"title":"","content":"For some more understanding of the situation, the PCs have made port on a small island in the Coral Archipelago to get the mast of the Dragonblood's ship fixed. It got snapped off by a ballista bolt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:22:38-07:00","id":1070511,"title":"","content":"What do they want to do with him, would be the main question for how to handle him, I'd say.<br /> <br /> A sneaky rather than loud escape attempt they can still interfere with can be a nice wrench thrown in the plans. If they want to try to convert him to their side and persuade him to give them a chance, write up some intimacies for him they can play off of.<br /> <br /> Ransoming him back might create an interesting plot event, dealing with an ambush by the ransomees to get him and their money back.<br /> <br /> If they're just leaving him in lockup and do nothing at all with him for a story or two, it's fair game to have them come back to their ship from a venture ashore to find a few crewmen knocked out and him nowhere in sight. He's not a helpless damsel just because he's a Dragon-Blooded, after all; he's a Prince of the Earth.<br /> <br /> But yeah, ask them what they think they want to do with him and plan around that. If they can convince him to work with them, build trust and loyalty and degrade his estimation of the Realm, that could be a fun way to pick up a unique retainer and enjoyable NPC to have around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:29:45-07:00","id":1070512,"title":"","content":"Hmm, honestly my first thought would be to try and escape to the sea, since water aspects can potentially breath underwater, so the guy might be able to get some distance that way.<br /> <br /> Okay how devout is this DB? What kind of skills and assets do they have, and the same for the DB?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:51:05-07:00","id":1070517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070512#post1070512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay how devout is this DB? What kind of skills and assets do they have, and the same for the DB?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he's not all that dogmatic with regards to the whole Solars/Anathema thing, although what he <i>is</i> is a sorcerer/historian who is devoted to the First Age. He's not dogmatic, but he has seen evidence of some of the atrocities which the ancient Solars committed, so he's not enormously well-disposed towards them.<br /> <br /> He's of House Iselsi, and hopes to find something in the West that could help restore his House's position somewhat in the coming storm. He's onto something too, as he managed to uncover a repository of documents from the First Age, which were previously kept in a magically-sealed box passed around as a curiosity in the West. Most important for him was a number of letters between an unknown Solar and Lunar referencing a First Age Manse which doesn't match up to any that the Dynasts already know of. He's been working on divining the Manse's position based on the dragon lines in the general area, and has been doing reasonably well, although he hasn't got it exactly. He was on his way back to the Isle to show what he'd found in person before he was *ahem* intercepted.<br /> <br /> For the Solars' assets, they've got six Solars, two of whom are sorcerers, a fast and ballista-equipped ship, a reasonably competent crew and backing from the Sealords of Coral. One of the sorcerers has an Erymanthus for a companion and both Summon Elemental and Summon First Circle Demon. Also, one of the Solars is a beastmaster-type with a giant rideable hawk. Don't ask.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for what they're planning to do with him, it's pretty much the third thing, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"756\" data-vbnamecard=\"756\">Meianno Yuurei</a> The thing is, though, that the island they're on, although it does have a small town, is really quite small, and given the Charms that they've got, they'd likely just recapture him. Seeing as he's a Terrestrial Sorcerer, and one working far away from people he wants to remain in contact with, him having the message-spell (I forget the proper name) would me reasonable, so he can almost certainly get a message out. To whom, though, was my issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-30-2017, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:58:05-07:00","id":1070518,"title":"","content":"Well if he's a terrestrial sorcerer he can probably get an elemental to help him out, or just fly away depending on his spells. He could call the nearest family outpost to relay word of his capture and findings. Would he be willing to sacrifice himself to get the data back to his family and out of the hands of the solars? Can he destroy the document or have the solars worked out where the manse is already?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:07:13-07:00","id":1070519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070518#post1070518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if he's a terrestrial sorcerer he can probably get an elemental to help him out, or just fly away depending on his spells. He could call the nearest family outpost to relay word of his capture and findings. Would he be willing to sacrifice himself to get the data back to his family and out of the hands of the solars? Can he destroy the document or have the solars worked out where the manse is already?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about the sacrifice, but he'd probably be able to escape via spells, as you said. The issue so far is that the Solars haven't left him alone, really, so he's chosen to keep his sorcery a secret so that he can use it without their stopping him. He could destroy the document, but one of the Solars who looked at the document has an eidetic memory. He wouldn't know that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:10:33-07:00","id":1070522,"title":"","content":"Either make him an asset or slay him.<br /> <br /> If you make him an asset, the most ideal circumstance would be to gain his loyalty, if that isn't possible then you could hostage him for a groovy ransom, or sell him to one of his enemies.<br /> <br /> Or if you really want to go out there, you could kill him and have a Neomah make his flesh into children using God, Animal, and or Exalt donors to add to it. Or if you want to be less creepy weird keep him prison with concubines who can get preggo, if it is a male DB anyways.<br /> <br /> Though if you kill him you could probably make his bones into Artifact Ingredients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:12:17-07:00","id":1070523,"title":"","content":"If he knows actual lore about solars he has to suspect that if they've seen the documents it's too late to keep things completely under wraps. That said a lot depends on wether he values escape, securing the manse for his family, or some other thing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:12:56-07:00","id":1070524,"title":"","content":"Hmm, what about hiring the PCs? I mean he wants to find this manse and once he does obviously various supplies and such will need to be directed at the place in order to set up an outpost on the place for study, reclamation, cleaning whatever horror has moved in while it's been abandoned, and so on and so forth. Of course these things could cause a potentially considerable uptick in ships with cargo, or other ships containing valuables that pirates may seek to appropriate for themselves. Of course no one gives a shit what happens to pirates, so the party would be free to attack these pirate ships at will and take what they want from the ships. <br /> <br /> Of course infallible messenger can be used to transmit where they're going after the DB ,and the party, figure out where the bloody place is which can lead to a rescue attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:15:08-07:00","id":1070525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070522#post1070522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if you really want to go out there, you could kill him and have a Neomah make his flesh into children using God, Animal, and or Exalt donors to add to it. Or if you want to be less creepy weird keep him prison with concubines who can get preggo, if it is a male DB anyways.<br /> <br /> Though if you kill him you could probably make his bones into Artifact Ingredients.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. That's just creepy weird overall. Plus, one of the Solars is a pretty devout priest of the Unconquered Sun and given ho he's behaved so far I don't think he'd go for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:20:08-07:00","id":1070526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070524#post1070524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what about hiring the PCs? I mean he wants to find this manse and once he does obviously various supplies and such will need to be directed at the place in order to set up an outpost on the place for study, reclamation, cleaning whatever horror has moved in while it's been abandoned, and so on and so forth. Of course these things could cause a potentially considerable uptick in ships with cargo, or other ships containing valuables that pirates may seek to appropriate for themselves. Of course no one gives a shit what happens to pirates, so the party would be free to attack these pirate ships at will and take what they want from the ships.<br /> <br /> Of course infallible messenger can be used to transmit where they're going after the DB ,and the party, figure out where the bloody place is which can lead to a rescue attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure with what he'd actually hire them. Money? They can get that from the Manse. The goodwill of the Realm? He's an Iselsi. Plunder from pirates? Same issue as the money.<br /> <br /> Also, for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11837\" data-vbnamecard=\"11837\">A Not Quite Simple Soul</a> , I'm not entirely sure whether he would be willing to sacrifice himself for his family. I'm thinking not, given te general mindset of House Iselsi - spies and blackguards - but he might, I guess.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Sorry about the double post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-30-2017, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:32:25-07:00","id":1070530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood#post1070506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so my players - who are pretty much a merry band of Solar pirates - have managed to capture a Water-Aspect Dragonblood after raiding his ship heading from the north West to the Blessed Isle. The issue is, I'm not entirely sure what to do with the character now. He's wise enough to know that just running from a group of 6 Solars is unlikely to end well for him, especially when one has a giant hawk he can ride on.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're at sea, right?<br /> <br /> And he's a Water Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:41:36-07:00","id":1070535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070530#post1070530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they're at sea, right?<br /> <br /> And he's a Water Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but TBH I don't have a vast amount of experience with Water aspects. Fire, Earth and Wood I've dealt with. Water not so much, and I've got not-very-much info with relation to Dragonblooded charms. i'm mainly making stuff up based on the QCs and stuff on the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:44:35-07:00","id":1070536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070526#post1070526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure with what he'd actually hire them. Money? They can get that from the Manse. The goodwill of the Realm? He's an Iselsi. Plunder from pirates? Same issue as the money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as you said he doesn't know the party has a person with a photographic memory, so as far as he knows he's the one with the information on any leads to the manse. So an offer of you scratch my back I scratch yours might help get them on grounds. At the very least the party would probably prefer him not fighting them every step of the way looking for the place and it's not like the dude is going to make this place any more lost if he's helping them figure out where it is. <br /> <br /> Yes they can potentially get stuff from the manse, but the party are in the same bag as the DB they don't know where it is. Plus they don't know what's in the manse, so a garuantee of pay ,with the potential for a bonus depending on how well claiming the manse goes, might go further along in getting them to cooperate with the guy than just the possibility of it having treasure and them having to do all the work themselves. So an offer of assistance finding it along with potentially getting loot out of it isn't a horrible offer. Not to mention Iselsi is the house that has a large network of informants and assassins. So the offer of either getting someone off their back in exchange for the job, or information on something/someone that they're looking for could also be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T01:46:57-07:00","id":1070537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070536#post1070536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well as you said he doesn't know the party has a person with a photographic memory, so as far as he knows he's the one with the information on any leads to the manse. So an offer of you scratch my back I scratch yours might help get them on grounds. At the very least the party would probably prefer him not fighting them every step of the way looking for the place and it's not like the dude is going to make this place any more lost if he's helping them figure out where it is.<br /> <br /> Yes they can potentially get stuff from the manse, but the party are in the same bag as the DB they don't know where it is. Plus they don't know what's in the manse, so a garuantee of pay ,with the potential for a bonus depending on how well claiming the manse goes, might go further along in getting them to cooperate with the guy than just the possibility of it having treasure and them having to do all the work themselves. So an offer of assistance finding it along with potentially getting loot out of it isn't a horrible offer. Not to mention Iselsi is the house that has a large network of informants and assassins. So the offer of either getting someone off their back in exchange for the job, or information on something/someone that they're looking for could also be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent points. Thanks very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T02:18:52-07:00","id":1070543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood#post1070506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">What to do with a Captured Dragonblood</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Chili if Fire aspect, caesar salad if Wood aspect, stew if Earth aspect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:09:58-07:00","id":1070548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070535#post1070535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but TBH I don't have a vast amount of experience with Water aspects. Fire, Earth and Wood I've dealt with. Water not so much, and I've got not-very-much info with relation to Dragonblooded charms. i'm mainly making stuff up based on the QCs and stuff on the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here's the thing. Their anima gives them power over water.<br /> <br /> In 2e they could swim really fast, breathe underwater, walk on water and perform normally impossible feats like underwater archery. If he was to escape he could just dive under the waves and there's very little your Solars could do to follow him barring a Saika familiar or some specialised sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:34:20-07:00","id":1070550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070535#post1070535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but TBH I don't have a vast amount of experience with Water aspects. Fire, Earth and Wood I've dealt with. Water not so much, and I've got not-very-much info with relation to Dragonblooded charms. i'm mainly making stuff up based on the QCs and stuff on the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Anima power of the Water Aspects can act and move in Water as easily as on land. Meaning they can run underwater, while most would treat it as difficult terrain, they can breath underwater, while most would drown, they can attack underwater while most would have a -3 penalty, and possibly another -3 penalty if they have to also fight the currant, and they can even fire arrows and throw things underwater.<br /> <br /> And when you include charms they can do even crazier things like high level turn my sailboat into a submarine power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:59:01-07:00","id":1070561,"title":"","content":"What about a non-trusting bargain sort of thing? Genre films and books have plenty of plots where characters that have no reason to trust each other are forced to work together to achieve a goal.<br /> <br /> Have him propose they help him find the Manse, because clearly they would want what's in it, too. He still thinks they are dangerous, and they know he's a Dragon-Blood, and would gladly call a Wyld Hunt on them.<br /> <br /> Over the next several sessions, it's up to the players to determine how to handle this. Maybe with careful social influence and trust in a clutch situation they can gain his true loyalty. if they are too harsh on their partner-prisoner, he may sabotage their plans at a crucial moment. Or maybe he sacrifices the Manse in an attempt to bury them at the end.<br /> <br /> I suggest this primarily because it gives the players the opportunity for extended roleplay and real decision making. Do they accept or reject his offer? Do they try to befriend him, or bully him? He can always escape later, creating a long-term antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  grammar 03-30-2017, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:01:05-07:00","id":1070562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070561#post1070561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a non-trusting bargain sort of things? Genre films and books have plenty of plots where characters that have no reason to trust each other are forced to work together to achieve a goal.<br /> <br /> Have him propose they help him find the Manse, because clearly they would want what's in it, too. He still thinks they are dangerous, and they know he's a Dragon-Blood, and would gladly call a Wyld Hunt on them.<br /> <br /> Over the next several sessions, it's up to the players to determine how to handle this. Maybe with careful social influence and trust in a clutch situation they can gain his true loyalty. if they are too harsh on their partner-prisoner, he may sabotage their plans at a crucial moment. Or maybe he sacrifices the Manse in an attempt to bury them at the end.<br /> <br /> I suggest this primarily because it gives the players the opportunity for extended roleplay and real decision making. Do they accept or reject his offer? Do they try to befriend him, or bully him? He can always escape later, creating a long-term antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent idea, and I think that combining it with the good <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a> 's would make for a very interesting situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:44:41-07:00","id":1070570,"title":"","content":"Burn 'em!<br /> <br /> #LytaWasRight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T04:54:59-07:00","id":1070576,"title":"","content":"There's good eatin' on one 'a them rich boys. Just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T05:38:28-07:00","id":1070581,"title":"","content":"OK, I used <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2093_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2093\" data-vbnamecard=\"2093\">Crumplepunch</a> 's rules for Dragonblood characters to whip up a 'character sheet' for Mr. Dragonblood (alias Iselsi Saraban). For reference, the Distant Horizon is the players' ship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8-xaAKdZ37vx4tUJabPZr3KiBtQpJeiKKHgsd0ALXc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8-xaAKdZ37vx4tUJabPZr3KiBtQpJeiKKHgsd0ALXc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8-xaAKdZ37vx4tUJabPZr3KiBtQpJeiKKHgsd0ALXc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8-xaAKdZ37vx4tUJabPZr3KiBtQpJeiKKHgsd0ALXc/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T05:50:48-07:00","id":1070591,"title":"","content":"Actually, I was planning to have another short plot-thing before getting on with finding the Manse (Surprise shadowland! Ghosts! Ghoulies! Stuff!) and it occurs to me that that would be a good way to form some kind of vaguely amiable understanding between the PCs and Saraban. The enemy of my enemy and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T06:22:38-07:00","id":1070602,"title":"","content":"What the solars should be doing is using social mechanics and charms and turn him over to their side. Shouldn't be too hard. Soon they should have a ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:14:18-07:00","id":1070621,"title":"","content":"So he is a smart Dragon-blooded sorcerer with an agenda.<br /> <br /> He just needs to make himself inconvenient enough that they should get rid of him. He is worth no money, no prestige. He is an Albatross hanging round their necks.<br /> <br /> Out of character I am astounded and happy to hear players taking prisoners. In some level, them letting him go is the best thing they can do to be rid of that anathema label. If they develop a reputation for being smart, merciful pirates reward them for it more often than punishing. It is the better market strategy, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:22:30-07:00","id":1070626,"title":"","content":"Eat the dragon's heart to gain his strength. <br /> <br /> [/onlyHalfJoking]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:54:45-07:00","id":1070709,"title":"","content":"Hmm... how knowledgable is the circle about the First Age? If they know more than him, he would be smart to at least play along (First Age Manses tend to be heavily defended and difficult to operate) to get at the manse more easily. Also the Anathema might have scraps of lore worth a king's ransom so an ambitious or desperate (he has got to be one or the other given what he is attempting alone) might tempt him as well.<br /> <br /> Just saying that a mutually beneficial arrangement and perhaps winning him over with information would not be the strangest thing given the character you described.<br /> <br /> Or they could offer his heart to the Unconquered. That totally would not be a waste of a rare opportunity.<br /> <br /> In either case some enchanted fishing nets might not be the worst thing to keep around just in case. Or if you have an Eclipse to bind him to a bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T10:25:47-07:00","id":1070729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070517#post1070517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, he's not all that dogmatic with regards to the whole Solars/Anathema thing, although what he <i>is</i> is a sorcerer/historian who is devoted to the First Age. He's not dogmatic, but he has seen evidence of some of the atrocities which the ancient Solars committed, so he's not enormously well-disposed towards them.<br /> <br /> He's of House Iselsi, and hopes to find something in the West that could help restore his House's position somewhat in the coming storm. He's onto something too, as he managed to uncover a repository of documents from the First Age, which were previously kept in a magically-sealed box passed around as a curiosity in the West. Most important for him was a number of letters between an unknown Solar and Lunar referencing a First Age Manse which doesn't match up to any that the Dynasts already know of. He's been working on divining the Manse's position based on the dragon lines in the general area, and has been doing reasonably well, although he hasn't got it exactly. He was on his way back to the Isle to show what he'd found in person before he was *ahem* intercepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone like that sounds like he'd go for something along the lines of... be polite to them, act like he's on their side (or has been convinced by them), cut deals with them if he can do so safely and help his own interests or family in the process, then (when it's safe to do so) turn around and stab them in the back for the good at the world.<br /> <br /> Obviously his ability to pull this off depends on his social skills and the skills of anyone in the group, but he has the advantage that he can be <i>mostly</i> honest (eg. he genuinely believes they're not demons and are capable of good, he genuinely wants to work with them, etc etc etc - depending on how he words it and what his intimacies are, it could be tricky for them to realize that he has an underlying belief that they're dangerous for the world and ultimately need to be stopped, since he could also genuinely think they're decent people and be willing to work with them on a short-term basis.)<br /> <br /> He would want to play up the idea that having a DB supporter to negotiate on their behalf could be useful, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T10:41:05-07:00","id":1070735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070709#post1070709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... how knowledgable is the circle about the First Age? If they know more than him, he would be smart to at least play along (First Age Manses tend to be heavily defended and difficult to operate) to get at the manse more easily. Also the Anathema might have scraps of lore worth a king's ransom so an ambitious or desperate (he has got to be one or the other given what he is attempting alone) might tempt him as well.<br /> <br /> Just saying that a mutually beneficial arrangement and perhaps winning him over with information would not be the strangest thing given the character you described.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, the PC circle know very little of the First Age. They've got two Twilights, one of whom concentrates much more on the <i>use</i> of sorcery than thescholarly study of it, and the other who would be more likely to know something. That said, the only real study in history he's had was as a scholar in Brightwork before it was taken over by the Coral Archipelago. If they didn't know it there, he doesn't know it, really. He might have <i>some</i> stuff about the First Age, but I'd wager not an enormous amount. <br /> <br /> As for whether the DB is more ambitious or desperate? I'm not really sure either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070709#post1070709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they could offer his heart to the Unconquered. That totally would not be a waste of a rare opportunity.<br /> <br /> In either case some enchanted fishing nets might not be the worst thing to keep around just in case. Or if you have an Eclipse to bind him to a bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Well, we do an Eclipse. No enchanted fishing nets, though (yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T10:41:48-07:00","id":1070738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070729#post1070729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone like that sounds like he'd go for something along the lines of... be polite to them, act like he's on their side (or has been convinced by them), cut deals with them if he can do so safely and help his own interests or family in the process, then (when it's safe to do so) turn around and stab them in the back for the good at the world.<br /> <br /> Obviously his ability to pull this off depends on his social skills and the skills of anyone in the group, but he has the advantage that he can be <i>mostly</i> honest (eg. he genuinely believes they're not demons and are capable of good, he genuinely wants to work with them, etc etc etc - depending on how he words it and what his intimacies are, it could be tricky for them to realize that he has an underlying belief that they're dangerous for the world and ultimately need to be stopped, since he could also genuinely think they're decent people and be willing to work with them on a short-term basis.)<br /> <br /> He would want to play up the idea that having a DB supporter to negotiate on their behalf could be useful, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty good to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:13:14-07:00","id":1070758,"title":"","content":"And if he's House Iselsi, he's definitely not in favor in the Realm, though his influence in the Threshold is probably significantly greater, given that people widely are in awe of Dragon-Blooded. That said, I would follow most of the recommendations in the thread that you've latched onto, but not be afraid to have him genuinely come round to be loyal to them, if they take it in that direction. As a sorcerer who is not a devout believer of the Immaculate Cult who is also a member of House Iselsi, it is entirely possible that he doesn't exactly <i>like</i> the current power structures of the Realm, and possibly of Creation. He may not have had the idea that &quot;I'm the center of all Creation&quot; as thoroughly beaten into his head as, say, a Mnemon or another, more powerful Great House would've. Those are really some of the bigger roadblocks to truly shifting a Dynast's opinion - if they can demonstrate that working with them is more beneficial to his aims (whether those are selfish, selfless, or House-bound), you could set up for a lot of conflict in him, if that's your style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:17:08-07:00","id":1070881,"title":"","content":"I think.... hummm... this is a tough call.... but I'm thinking a jasmine tea to start. Of course you need the cucumber sandwiches to go with it, it's not a proper tea time without them. And then follow up with a polite discussion about the weather, the crops of course... perhaps if he's familiar with that one lovely little tea house in Steel Lotus just off the street of silver artificers.<br /> <br /> And then after things are settled a bit, ASK him what he would like you to do with him, given the whole almost-at-war situation between the Anathema and the dragonblooded.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:55:40-07:00","id":1070903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070526#post1070526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure with what he'd actually hire them. Money? They can get that from the Manse.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou can never have too much money.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goodwill of the Realm? He's an Iselsi.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOpenly? A lot of Iselsi go by assumed identities.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, there's the question of whether the good will of the Iselsi in this case is worth anything.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the core of the question, I'm thinking... nobody on a ship is allowed to get by without pulling their weight.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, a Water Aspect can survive in the ocean, but... are they going to walk or swim for hundreds of miles?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:14:23-07:00","id":1070910,"title":"","content":"As I am given to understand, the following steps should be taken:<ul><li>Shave his belly with a rusty razor</li> <li>Put him in a long boat 'til he's sober</li> <li>Stick him in a scrubber with a hosepipe on him</li> <li>Put him in bed with the captain's daughter</li> </ul><br /> I'm pretty sure that's proper naval procedure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:09:53-07:00","id":1070936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1070910#post1070910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I am given to understand, the following steps should be taken:<ul><li>Shave his belly with a rusty razor</li> <li>Put him in a long boat 'til he's sober</li> <li>Stick him in a scrubber with a hosepipe on him</li> <li>Put him in bed with the captain's daughter</li> </ul><br /> I'm pretty sure that's proper naval procedure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er'lye in the mornin'!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:02:12-07:00","id":1071465,"title":"","content":"You know what could really help his House?<br /> <br /> Having some God-Kings for friends. Six of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T17:07:57-07:00","id":1071509,"title":"","content":"I've found it helpful for the Realm houses to use a form of &quot;honor currency&quot; - special artifact jade coins that aren't worth a particularly large amount of money, but that can be redeemed no-questions-asked for favors by the house granting them. So, you give one of their heirs back, plus his artifact gear? That's worth a few coins, sure - and there's a banked plot for future use.<br /> <br /> They aren't meant to be traded to soulless Anathema abominations, of course - they're <i>meant</i> to be used to ransom stuff back from another House. But... there <i>is</i> a lot of personal pride and institutional credit bound up in honoring them; will they still be respected if a Solar comes to collect? Who knows, but it'll probably be interesting to find out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:32:31-07:00","id":1073456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1071509#post1071509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found it helpful for the Realm houses to use a form of &quot;honor currency&quot; - special artifact jade coins that aren't worth a particularly large amount of money, but that can be redeemed no-questions-asked for favors by the house granting them. So, you give one of their heirs back, plus his artifact gear? That's worth a few coins, sure - and there's a banked plot for future use.<br /> <br /> They aren't meant to be traded to soulless Anathema abominations, of course - they're <i>meant</i> to be used to ransom stuff back from another House. But... there <i>is</i> a lot of personal pride and institutional credit bound up in honoring them; will they still be respected if a Solar comes to collect? Who knows, but it'll probably be interesting to find out!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a cool idea. Also, there's no guarantee the person given the favor tokens knows the giver is a Solar. If I travel halfway across Creation and show some rando House member my cred, it's unlikely he knows about how I acquired them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:28:59-07:00","id":1073505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1073456#post1073456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a cool idea. Also, there's no guarantee the person given the favor tokens knows the giver is a Solar. If I travel halfway across Creation and show some rando House member my cred, it's unlikely he knows about how I acquired them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In full disclosure, the idea's stolen from elsewhere, but it's worked out pretty well in my game so far. Solves the &quot;too many jade daiklaves&quot; problem neatly, among other benefits.<br /> <br /> And that's true! Some dude walks up to him and says, &quot;Hey, do you want to earn an honor coin?&quot; - his first thought is probably not to check for Anathema. (I can't help picturing that playing out sort of like the John Wick assassin currency, now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T20:19:07-07:00","id":1073531,"title":"","content":"It's not a bad idea, I've seen a lot of works where favors are traded in an almost literal capacity, so you could certainly extrapolate it out. Various markings on a coin to denote which house, maybe member if a person is particularly prominent, and the level of the favor. Heck you could go a step further and have a few spirits or sorcerers in the houses who include part of their job being to do something to sanctify a marker to establish that it is a legit favor the house owes someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T07:25:00-07:00","id":1074115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1070506-what-to-do-with-a-captured-dragonblood?p=1073505#post1073505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In full disclosure, the idea's stolen from elsewhere, but it's worked out pretty well in my game so far. Solves the &quot;too many jade daiklaves&quot; problem neatly, among other benefits.<br /> <br /> And that's true! Some dude walks up to him and says, &quot;Hey, do you want to earn an honor coin?&quot; - his first thought is probably not to check for Anathema. (I can't help picturing that playing out sort of like the John Wick assassin currency, now.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as you mentioned it, my mind conjured up a Night Caste, wearing all black, walking into a Dynast pleasure dome with a valise of jade coins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}